+/* Experimental host-picture import; not a stable upstream ABI.
+ * Input is planar YUV420P, 8 or 10 bits, with positive aligned strides.
+ * data_size[i] is the accessible allocation size starting at data[i],
+ * including complete padded rows and at least 64 trailing readable bytes.
+ * All data pointers and strides must be aligned to 32 bytes. Dimensions
+ * must be even. Caller must keep pixel data unchanged until release(cookie).
+ * On success, release runs exactly once on the last picture unref, possibly
+ * from a worker thread. On failure, ownership stays with the caller, release
+ * is not called, and *pic is unchanged. Do not overwrite a live picture.
+ * This validates storage, not arbitrary feature-extractor compatibility.
